HTTPS specification
HTTP [RFC2616] was originally used in the clear on the Internet. However, increased use of HTTP for sensitive applications has required security measures. SSL, and its successor TLS [RFC2246] were designed to provide channel-oriented security.
&lt;a href=&quot;https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2818&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2818&lt;/a&gt;</skos:definition>
