  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainApplicationComponent_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-20</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Blockchain ABB is an Application Component that implements a set of rules and processes to enable secure and transparent transactions and record-keeping for sharing of information, enabling permanent, immutable, and transparent recording of data and transactions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Blockchain</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Blockchain</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:BlockchainApplicationComponent</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Fishcoin Project, is a project using Blockchain technologies for seafood traceability. https://fishcoin.co/</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainApplicationComponent</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in European Blockchain Strategy</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Blockchain Application Component ABB is salient for interoperability because it implements a set of elements needed and used by blockchain services. Those aspects are peer network, smart contracts, membership, events, ledger, system integration, wallet, and system management. All listed components can be part of a digital public service enhancing trustability and enabling interoperability in a secure and reliable way.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainApplicationComponent"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainApplicationComponent_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainApplicationComponent</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/library/european-blockchain-strategy-brochure</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note>In the creation of the Blockchain component, several actors such as developer, user, architect, regulator, operator, membership services, etc. are present in a blockchain that provides a solution to a blockchain-based business network. Each actor and component present in a blockchain plays a major role to make the network more secure and reliable.</skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainApplicationService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-20</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Blockchain ABB is an Application Service that enables secure, transparent, and immutable record-keeping and transaction processing shared by all participants in a network.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Blockchain</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Blockchain</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:BlockchainApplicationService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Fishcoin Project, is a project using Blockchain technologies for seafood traceability. https://fishcoin.co/</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainApplicationService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in European Comission-Blockchain Strategy</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Blockchain Application Service ABB is salient for interoperability because as a ledger technology application service can contribute to the trustability of digital public services. It can enable the register and list of irrevocable transactional data being exchanged between digital public services. To that extent, a blockchain service can be enhancing digital public services by establishing a mechanism to track data, and the process applied to it.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainApplicationService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainApplicationService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainApplicationService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/blockchain-strategy</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note>Specifically, Blockchain  stores records that contain a time stamp and reference links to previous transactions. With this information, anyone with access rights can trace back a transactional event, at any point in its history, belonging to any participant. A blockchain is one architectural design of the broader concept of distributed ledgers.</skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainEnablersGrouping_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Blockchain Enablers ABB is a Grouping that refers to components and services that facilitate the development, deployment, and management of ledger technology applications</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Blockchain Enablers</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Blockchain Enablers</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:BlockchainEnablersGrouping</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Fishcoin Project, is a project using Blockchain technologies for seafood traceability. https://fishcoin.co/</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainEnablersGrouping</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in European Blockchain Strategy</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Blockchain Enablers Grouping ABB is salient for interoperability because it comprises the tools, applications and services relevant to implement and deploying ledger technologies into digital public services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainEnablersGrouping"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/library/european-blockchain-strategy-brochure</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainEnablersGrouping_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainEnablersGrouping</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainInfrastructureEnablers_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Blockchain Infrastructure Enablers ABB is a Grouping of a set of components and services that permit building a digital ledger infrastructure of interconnected nodes to facilitate a trustworthy environment to share data.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Blockchain Infrastructure Enablers</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Blockchain Infrastructure Enablers</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:BlockchainInfrastructureEnablers</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): OpenCHAIN is an open-source blockchain platform with distributed ledger technology. This blockchain company is suitable for organizations managing digital assets in secure and robust ways. Blockchain technology does not require fees for mining and the Bitcoin blockchain is significant for its immutability. https://www.openchainproject.org/</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainInfrastructureEnablers</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>European Comission</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Blockchain Infrastructure Enablers ABB is salient for organizational interoperability due to it setting up the rules for generating a trustworthy network that permits (i) sharing information related to public services securely and privately, and (ii) ensuring the public information is consistent in time.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainInfrastructureEnablers"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainInfrastructureEnablers</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainInfrastructureEnablers_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/european-blockchain-services-infrastructure</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainLedgerTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Blockchain Ledger ABB is a Technology Service that enables the procedures to record, share, and synchronize transactions in the respective electronic ledger.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Blockchain Ledger</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Blockchain Ledger</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:BlockchainLedgerTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): OpenCHAIN is an open-source blockchain platform with distributed ledger technology. This blockchain company is suitable for organizations managing digital assets in secure and robust ways. Blockchain technology does not require fees for mining and the Bitcoin blockchain is significant for its immutability. https://www.openchainproject.org/</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainLedgerTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>World Bank</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Blockchain Ledger ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it established the elements to publish public services and subsequent information securely across a trustworthy network.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainLedgerTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainLedgerTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BlockchainLedgerTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.worldbank.org/en/topic/financialsector/brief/blockchain-dlt</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note>Electronic Ledgers means the electronic master records of all contracts of the Sellers or the Issuer similar to and including the Contracts</skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

