        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">DEFINITION:
Code of ethics compliance ABB is a Principle refering to the expression of important values and standards that are also to be found in the law, but are not encumbered by the limitations and constraints that necessarily attach to legally-binding rules that can be used to impose sanctions.

Source: Investopaidia
(&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/code-of-ethics.asp#:~:text=Compliance-based%20codes%20of%20ethics%20not%20only%20set%20guidelines,codes%20of%20ethics%20to%20enforce%20laws%20and%20regulations&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/code-of-ethics.asp#:~:text=Complia…&lt;/a&gt;.)

EXAMPLES:
The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB):</skos:definition>
