  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestReport_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Conformance Test Report</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Conformance Test Report</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:ConformanceTestReport</dc:type>
    <eira:ID>ABB131</eira:ID>
    <eira:ABB_Status>Obsolete</eira:ABB_Status>
    <owl:deprecated>true</owl:deprecated>
    <skos:related>
      <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestReport">
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">DEFINITION:
Conformance Test Report ABB is a Business Object testing activities and subsequently consolidated in a report to inform stakeholders.

Source: ISTQB
(&lt;a href=&quot;http://glossary.istqb.org/search/test&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://glossary.istqb.org/search/test&lt;/a&gt;)

Syn. Test results

INTEROPERABILITY SALIENCY:
IoP Dimension: Structural IoP
The Conformance Test Report ABB &amp;nbsp;is salient for technical interoperability because it provides reports of data testing to inform stakeholders.

EXAMPLES:
The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB):

Jenkins jUnit plug-in

The JUnit plugin provides a publisher that consumes XML test reports generated during the builds and provides some graphical visualization of the historical test results (see JUnit graph for a sample) as well as a web UI for viewing test reports, tracking failures, and so on. Jenkins understands the JUnit test report XML format (which is also used by TestNG). When this option is configured, Jenkins can provide useful information about test results, such as trends.

Source: (&lt;a href=&quot;https://wiki.jenkins.io/display/JENKINS/JUnit+Plugin&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://wiki.jenkins.io/display/JENKINS/JUnit+Plugin&lt;/a&gt;)</skos:definition>
        <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Conformance Test Report</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Deprecated"/>
        <owl:deprecated>true</owl:deprecated>
      </skos:Concept>
    </skos:related>

    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestReport_Properties</dc:identifier>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestScenarioBusinessObject_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-18</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Conformance Test Scenario ABB is a Business Object specifying a sequence of actions for the execution of a test. Also known as a test script or manual test script.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Conformance Test Scenario</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Conformance Test Scenario</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:ConformanceTestScenarioBusinessObject</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): SoapUI - SoapUI is the world's most widely-used open source API testing tool for SOAP and REST APIs. SoapUI offers SOAP Web Services functional testing, REST API functional testing, WSDL coverage, message assertion testing and test refactoring. Scenario-based tests should be directly tied to user stories, which were probably provided by the product owner or some business stakeholder. Under ideal circumstances, these tests should be the user stories, so that business stakeholders can both easily help the tester develop the test cases and understand the results. [https://www.soapui.org/testing-dojo/best-practices/scenario-based-testing.html][https://www.soapui.org/testing-dojo/world-of-api-testing/test-first.html]</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestScenarioBusinessObject</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>NIST</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Conformance Testing Scenario ABB  is salient for technical interoperability because it provides a document of a list of activities for the execution of interoperability tests.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestScenarioBusinessObject"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestScenarioBusinessObject_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestScenarioBusinessObject</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.nist.gov/itl/ssd/information-systems-group/overview-conformance-testing</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestingApplicationComponent_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-18</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Conformance Testing ABB is an Application Component that enables a structural and modular approach for implementing the validation of the application or service to meet the requirements of a standard or specification</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Conformance Testing</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Conformance Testing</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:ConformanceTestingApplicationComponent</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Interoperability Testbed - The Test Bed allows users to execute predefined test cases on their systems in order to test the conformance to standards and requirements, simulate a web-service, validate content and test a complete message exchange protocol. The Testbed manages test cases and users, and orchestrates domain-specific components, the domain-specific logic is in separate components that are used via web services. Test results are provided in a standardised, machine-readable format. The Test Bed also offers a test registry and repository (TRR) to store test artefacts (assertions, test cases, validation schemas, etc.) and compile test services (validation services, simulator services, etc.). Please visit the following website for more information: https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/interoperability-test-bed_en</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestingApplicationComponent</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Governance IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>NIST</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Conformance Testing Component ABB  is salient for technical interoperability because it enables the validation and verification that several solutions at one or more layers of the interoperability stack and they satisfy certain interoperability requirements.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestingApplicationComponent"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestingApplicationComponent_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestingApplicationComponent</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.nist.gov/itl/ssd/information-systems-group/conformance-testing</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestingApplicationService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-18</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Conformance Testing ABB is an Application Service that enables the activities and rules to determine whether a tool, platform or service faithfully meets the requirements of a standard or specification</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Conformance Testing</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Conformance Testing</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:ConformanceTestingApplicationService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Interoperability Testbed - The Test Bed allows users to execute predefined test cases on their systems in order to test the conformance to standards and requirements, simulate a web-service, validate content and test a complete message exchange protocol. The Testbed manages test cases and users, and orchestrates domain-specific components, the domain-specific logic is in separate components that are used via web services. Test results are provided in a standardised, machine-readable format. The Test Bed also offers a test registry and repository (TRR) to store test artefacts (assertions, test cases, validation schemas, etc.) and compile test services (validation services, simulator services, etc.). Please visit the following website for more information: https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/solutions/interoperability-test-bed_en</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestingApplicationService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>NIST</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Conformance Testing Services ABB  is salient for technical interoperability because it enables the validation and verification that several solutions at one or more layers of the interoperability stack and they satisfy certain interoperability requirements.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestingApplicationService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.nist.gov/itl/ssd/information-systems-group/conformance-testing</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestingApplicationService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestingApplicationService</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note>The logistics of interoperability testing is usually more costly (time, coordination, interoperability), and interoperability testing is no substitute for a conformance test suite. Experience shows that interoperability testing is more successful and less costly when conformance of implementations has been tested first.</skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainerInfrastructureEnablers_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Containers Infrastructure Enabler ABB is a Grouping of components and services enabling a virtual packaging code and isolated applications for deployment of public services.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Containers Infrastructure Enablers</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Containers Infrastructure Enablers</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:ContainerInfrastructureEnablers</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): OpenSHIFT is a secure and an enterprise-grade cloud-based container orchestration system with Kubernetes at the backend. It can be used both as a Red Hat Container Orchestration Engine and Platform-as-a-Service (PaaS). https://github.com/openshift/origin</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainerInfrastructureEnablers</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in referent cloud service providers</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Containers Infrastructure Enablers ABB is salient for organizational interoperability due to setting up the rules and business process to establish and manage the virtual tools that permit determining the functionality of the public digital services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainerInfrastructureEnablers"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainerInfrastructureEnablers</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainerInfrastructureEnablers_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference></eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainerRegistryTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Containers Registry ABB is a Technology Service that enables the procedures to elaborate a repository of a collection of registries used to store and access container images</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Container Registry</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Container Registry</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:ContainerRegistryTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Project QUAY, Quay is a container image registry that enables you to build, organize, distribute, and deploy containers. Quay gives you security over your repositories with image vulnerability scanning and robust access controls. Project Quay provides a scalable open source platform to host container images across any size organization. https://www.projectquay.io/</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainerRegistryTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>Redhat</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Container Registry ABB is salient for semantic interoperability due to it establishing a catalogue of registries of virtual public services and tools to be deployed and executed.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainerRegistryTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.redhat.com/en/topics/cloud-native-apps/what-is-a-container-registry</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainerRegistryTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainerRegistryTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainerSystemSoftware_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-31</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Container ABB is a Technology Service that implements an executable unit of software in which application code is packaged, along with its libraries and dependencies, in common ways so that it can be run anywhere, whether it be on a desktop, traditional IT, or the cloud</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Container</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Container</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:ContainerSystemSoftware</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Docker. Docker is a containerization technology that works with the Kubernetes platform, with many adopting it to create an app that runs across multiple containers. https://www.docker.com/</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainerSystemSoftware</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in referent cloud service providers</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Container ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it provides the packaged software that contains or nurtures the functionalities of public services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainerSystemSoftware"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainerSystemSoftware_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainerSystemSoftware</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference></eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainersManagerTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Containers Manager ABB is a Technology Service that implements the process of organizing, adding or replacing large numbers of software containers</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Containers Manager</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Containers Manager</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:ContainersManagerTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): OpenSHIFT is a secure and an enterprise-grade cloud-based container orchestration system with Kubernetes at the backend. It can be used both as a Red Hat Container Orchestration Engine and Platform-as-a-Service (PaaS). https://github.com/openshift/origin</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainersManagerTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in referent cloud service providers</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Containers Manager ABB is salient for technical interoperability due to its setting up the software tool to manage virtual public services and tools.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainersManagerTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainersManagerTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainersManagerTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference></eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainersOrchestratorTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Containers Orchestration ABB is a Technology Service that enables the procedures to automate the deployment, management, scaling, and networking of containers</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Containers Orchestrator</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Containers Orchestrator</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:ContainersOrchestratorTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): OpenSHIFT is a secure and an enterprise-grade cloud-based container orchestration system with Kubernetes at the backend. It can be used both as a Red Hat Container Orchestration Engine and Platform-as-a-Service (PaaS). https://github.com/openshift/origin</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainersOrchestratorTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>Red Hat</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Containers Orchestrator ABB is salient for technical interoperability due to it provides the mechanism and networks to organize virtual public services and tools to facilitate the deployment and publication of public digital services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainersOrchestratorTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.redhat.com/en/topics/containers/what-is-container-orchestration</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainersOrchestratorTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContainersOrchestratorTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContentDeliveryInfrastructureEnablers_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Content Delivery Infrastructure Enablers ABB is a Grouping that refers to the set of components and services that enable the delivery of digital content such as web pages, videos, images, and audio files to end-users</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Content Delivery Infrastructure Enablers</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Content Delivery Infrastructure Enablers</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:ContentDeliveryInfrastructureEnablers</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): DIGIT/C Hosting Service - DIGIT/C offers a high availability and high performance hosting infrastructure that is being comprised, among other elements, of back-end web server instances and application servers for hosting and serving both static and dynamic sites. http://ec.europa.eu/ipg/build/infrastructure/index_en.htm</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContentDeliveryInfrastructureEnablers</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in the definition provided by relebant cloud service organizations.</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Content Delivery Infrastructure Enablers ABB is salient for semantic and technical interoperability because it provides ICT systems to manipulate, reuse and share batch and streaming data related to public administration services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContentDeliveryInfrastructureEnablers"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContentDeliveryInfrastructureEnablers</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContentDeliveryInfrastructureEnablers_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference></eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ContentManagementComponent_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Content Management Component</skos:notation>
