  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceApplicationComponent_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-20</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Digital Workplace ABB is an Application Component that enables the implementation of the procedures to freely collaborate independently from the location and boundaries while maintaining high-security standards and increasing productivity and efficiency.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Digital Workplace</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Digital Workplace</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:DigitalWorkplaceApplicationComponent</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Set of IT tools used by European Commission officials, workers, etc. There is a new strategy put in place by the Commission to improve the work of the different roles involved. https://europa.eu/digitec/news/digital-workplace-european-commission/</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceApplicationComponent</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>European Comission</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Digital Workplace Application Component ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it provides the components and tools that allow the free collaboration of staffing people while maintaining high-security standards.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceApplicationComponent"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://ec.europa.eu/info/publications/digital-workplace-strategy_en</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceApplicationComponent_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceApplicationComponent</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceApplicationService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-20</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Digital Workplace ABB is an Application Service that enables the procedures to freely collaborate independently from the location and boundaries while maintaining high-security standards and increasing productivity and efficiency.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Digital Workplace</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Digital Workplace</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:DigitalWorkplaceApplicationService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Set of IT tools used by European Commission officials, workers, etc. There is a new strategy put in place by the Commission to improve the work of the different roles involved. https://europa.eu/digitec/news/digital-workplace-european-commission/</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceApplicationService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>European Comission</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:viewpoint>Key Interoperability Enablers viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Digital Workplace Application Service ABB is a key interoperability enabler (*) for behavioural and technical interoperability by enabling components for free collaboration and accessibility to public services, maintaining high-security standards.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceApplicationService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceApplicationService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceApplicationService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://ec.europa.eu/info/publications/digital-workplace-strategy_en</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceEnablersGrouping_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Digital Workplace Enablers is a Grouping that refers to components or services that enable the collaboration of work aspects while security and privacy are ensured.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Digital Workplace Enablers</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Digital Workplace Enablers</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:DigitalWorkplaceEnablersGrouping</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Set of IT tools used by European Commission officials, workers, etc. There is a new strategy put in place by the Commission to improve the work of the different roles involved. https://europa.eu/digitec/news/digital-workplace-european-commission/</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceEnablersGrouping</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>European Comission</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Digital Workplace Enablers Grouping ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it tools, components or services that allow the free collaboration of work aspects while security and privacy are ensured. The free collaboration is relevant for interoperability because allows to enable and maintain digital public services without the need of being at the Organisation responsible for digital public services head quarters</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceEnablersGrouping"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceEnablersGrouping_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceEnablersGrouping</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://ec.europa.eu/info/publications/digital-workplace-strategy_en</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceInfrastructureEnablers_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Digital Workplace Infrastructure Enablers ABB is a Grouping that enables the set of components and services that enable organizations to create and manage virtual workplaces environments and facilitate their access remotely.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Digital Workplace Infrastructure Enablers</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Digital Workplace Infrastructure Enablers</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:DigitalWorkplaceInfrastructureEnablers</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): PSI Remote Desktop Service from the European Open Science Cloud https://marketplace.eosc-portal.eu/services/remote-desktop-service?from_recommendation_panel=true&amp;fromc=access-physical-einfrastructures</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceInfrastructureEnablers</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in Gartner</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Digital Workplace Infrastructure Enablers ABB is salient for technical interoperability due to it refers to setting up the workplace ecosystem to establish access to European public services remotely to access applications using open specifications and interfaces.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceInfrastructureEnablers"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceInfrastructureEnablers_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalWorkplaceInfrastructureEnablers</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.gartner.com/en/information-technology/glossary/remote-access</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalisationRoadmapWorkPackage_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-12-1</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Digitaliation Roadmap ABB is a Work Package that corresponds to a high-level vision and strategy referring to long-term business goal an organization wants to achieve, including digital initiatives and goals the organization will drive.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Digitalisation Roadmap</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Digitalisation Roadmap</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:DigitalisationRoadmapWorkPackage</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Digital roadmap for organising mobility authorities (OMAs). (https://cerre.eu/publications/mobility-as-a-service-maas-digital-roadmap-public-transport-authorities/)</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalisationRoadmapWorkPackage</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in referent consultancy companies and IEEE</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Governance IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Digitalization Roadmap ABB is salient for the governance, semantic and technical interoperability because it commonly offers (i) a transversal vision of existing reusable standards applied in the digitalization of the public sector, (ii) actions to ensure data exchange between digital services; (iii) technological software and assets that should be included in the digitalization of public administrations.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:viewpoint>Interoperability Governance viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalisationRoadmapWorkPackage"/>
    <eira:view>Organisational view</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalisationRoadmapWorkPackage</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalisationRoadmapWorkPackage_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://roadmaps.ieee.org/guide-to-technology-roadmaps</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DiscoveryandRegistryServiceApplicationService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-18</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Service Discovery and Registry ABB is an Application Service that enables the process of automatically locating network services within distributed digital systems.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Service Discovery and Registry</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Service Discovery and Registry</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:DiscoveryandRegistryServiceApplicationService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): ZooKeeper - ZooKeeper is a centralized service registry for maintaining configuration information, naming, providing distributed synchronization, and providing group services. All of these kinds of services are used in some form or another by distributed applications. Each time they are implemented there is a lot of work that goes into fixing the bugs and race conditions that are inevitable. Because of the difficulty of implementing these kinds of services, applications initially usually skimp on them, which make them brittle in the presence of change and difficult to manage. Even when done correctly, different implementations of these services lead to management complexity when the applications are deployed. https://zookeeper.apache.org/</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DiscoveryandRegistryServiceApplicationService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in INSPIRE</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:viewpoint>Key Interoperability Enablers viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Service Discovery and Registry Service ABB is a key interoperability enabler (*) for structural and behavioural interoperability by enabling access rights for data that is necessary for accessing public administration components to target fast and easy communication and data exchange.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DiscoveryandRegistryServiceApplicationService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DiscoveryandRegistryServiceApplicationService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DiscoveryandRegistryServiceApplicationService</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://inspire.ec.europa.eu/glossary/DiscoveryService</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DistributedBlockchainNetworkTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>stributed Blockchain Network ABB is a Technology Service that enables the implementation procedures to manage tokens that may be utilised and/or exchanged, as communicated by the Company to the Token holders from time to time</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Distributed Blockchain Network</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Distributed Blockchain Network</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:DistributedBlockchainNetworkTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Oasis Network, The Oasis Network is a Layer 1 decentralized blockchain network designed to be uniquely scalable, privacy-first and versatile. The Network has two main architectural components, the consensus layer and the ParaTime layer: 1. The consensus layer is a scalable, high-throughput, secure, proof-of-stake consensus run by a decentralized set of validator nodes; 2. The ParaTime layer hosts many parallel runtimes (ParaTimes), each representing a replicated compute environment with shared state. https://docs.oasis.io/general/oasis-network/</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DistributedBlockchainNetworkTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>World Bank</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Distributed Blockchain Network ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it establishes the infrastructure to share information and also makes the information consistent under distributed data stores.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DistributedBlockchainNetworkTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DistributedBlockchainNetworkTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DistributedBlockchainNetworkTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.worldbank.org/en/topic/financialsector/brief/blockchain-dlt</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DistributedFileSystemTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Distributed File System is a Technology Service that implements the behaviour of a software tool that allows access to files from multiple computers in a distributed network</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Distributed File System</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Distributed File System</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:DistributedFileSystemTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): MooseFS is a Fault-tolerant, Highly available, Highly performing, Scaling-out, Network distributed file system. It spreads data over several physical commodity servers, which are visible to the user as one virtual disk. It is POSIX compliant and acts like any other Unix-like file system supporting: -Hierarchical structure: Files and Folders, -File attributes, -Special files: Pipes, Sockets, Block and Character devices, -Symbolic and Hard links, -Security attributes and ACLs. https://moosefs.com/</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DistributedFileSystemTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in Gartner</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopSaliency></eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DistributedFileSystemTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.gartner.com/reviews/market/distributed-file-systems-and-object-storage</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DistributedFileSystemTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DistributedFileSystemTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DistributedLedgerDataObject_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-17</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Distributed Ledger ABB is a Data Object that enables the sharing and recording of encrypted data across multiple sites, countries, or institutions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Distributed Ledger</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Distributed Ledger</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:DistributedLedgerDataObject</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): TOLAR (https://tolar.io/)is a tool implemented as the outcome of the Seduproject, Hashnet is in the process of evaluation by the European Blockchain Partnership to become one of the pilot protocols for European Blockchain Service Infrastructure. https://www.seedeuproject.eu/partners/hashnet/</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DistributedLedgerDataObject</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>Regulation of a pilot regime for market infrastructures based on distributed ledger technology</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Distributed Ledger ABB is salient for semantic interoperability due to its capacity to exchange encrypted data amongst digital public services. It is also salient because it can be used across borders to ensure secure and trustworthy data exchange. Additionally, it is also relevant for new technologies incorporating blockchain technology.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DistributedLedgerDataObject"/>
    <eira:view>Semantic view</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DistributedLedgerDataObject_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DistributedLedgerDataObject</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:52020PC0594&amp;from=EN</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DocumentManagementService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Document Management Service</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Document Management Service</skos:prefLabel>
