  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EdgeComputingTechnologyCollaboration_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-31</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Edge Computing ABB is a Technology Collaboration that enables the procedures to implement a distributed computing topology where information processing is located close to the edge, where things and people produce or consume that information</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Edge Computing</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Edge Computing</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:EdgeComputingTechnologyCollaboration</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): SovereignEDGE.eu https://sovereignedge.eu/</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EdgeComputingTechnologyCollaboration</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>Gartner</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Edge Computing ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it provides needed computational elements and tools to perform data analytics in specific devices that can nurture public administration digital services (e.g. mobiles from citizens).</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EdgeComputingTechnologyCollaboration"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EdgeComputingTechnologyCollaboration_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EdgeComputingTechnologyCollaboration</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.gartner.com/en/information-technology/glossary/edge-computing</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifInteroperabilityLevelBusinessObject_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-23</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>EIF Interoperability Level ABB is a Business Object setting guidelines for developing public services. The EIF defines four interoperability levels, which cover legal, organisational, semantic and technical interoperability. Each level deserves special attention when a new European public service is established.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of EIF Interoperability Level</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of EIF Interoperability Level</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:EifInteroperabilityLevelBusinessObject</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): The EIF defines four interoperability levels, which cover legal, organisational, semantic and technical interoperability.</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifInteroperabilityLevelBusinessObject</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopDimension>Governance IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>European Commission, ISA Programme. The New European Interoperability Framework (EIF) for European public services. [Online] 2017</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:viewpoint>EIRA Ontology viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency></eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifInteroperabilityLevelBusinessObject"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifInteroperabilityLevelBusinessObject_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifInteroperabilityLevelBusinessObject</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>(https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/eif_en.)</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifPrinciple_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-23</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>EIF Principle ABB is a Principle analysing European Public Services by driving the identification and formulation of interoperability requirements with higher levels of granularity and used to design European public services by driving the identification and formulation of interoperability specifications</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of EIF Principle</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of EIF Principle</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:EifPrinciple</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Transparency: EIF Transparency Principle refers to: 1. Enabling visibility inside the administrative environment of a public administration. This is about allowing other public administrations, citizens and businesses to view and understand administrative rules, processes, data, services and decision-making.  2. Ensuring availability of interfaces with internal information systems. Public administrations operate a large number of what are often heterogeneous and disparate information systems in support of their internal processes. Interoperability depends on ensuring the availability of interfaces to these systems and the data they handle. In turn, interoperability facilitates reuse of systems and data, and enables these to be integrated into larger systems. 3. Securing the right to the protection of personal data, by respecting the applicable legal framework for the large volumes of personal data of citizens, held and managed by Public administrations.(https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/default/files/eif_brochure_final.pdf)</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifPrinciple</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>EIF</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopSaliency></eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:viewpoint>Interoperability Security viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:viewpoint>Interoperability Privacy viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:viewpoint>EIRA Ontology viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:viewpoint>Key Interoperability Enablers viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifPrinciple"/>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/eif_en</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifPrinciple_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EifPrinciple</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EiraArchitectureBuildingBlock_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of EIRA Architecture Building Block</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of EIRA Architecture Building Block</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:EiraArchitectureBuildingBlock</dc:type>
    <eira:ID>ABB337</eira:ID>
    <eira:ABB_Status>Obsolete</eira:ABB_Status>
    <owl:deprecated>true</owl:deprecated>
    <skos:related>
      <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EiraArchitectureBuildingBlock">
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">DEFINITION:
EIRA Architecture Building Block ABB is a Business Object acting as a requirement of an intermediate  level of granularity, in alignment with at least one EIF principle, formulated as an agreed normative statement in functional terms on a legal, organisational, semantic, or technical attribute of a To-Be European Public Service. An EIRA ABB might encapsulate several interoperability aspects

Source: Europa
(&lt;a href=&quot;https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/display/CEFDIGITAL/What+is+a+Building+Block&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/display/CEFDIGITAL/W…&lt;/a&gt;)

EXAMPLES:
The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB):

A Legal Act is an EIRA Architecture Building Block from a Legal view perspective.</skos:definition>
        <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">EIRA Architecture Building Block</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Deprecated"/>
        <owl:deprecated>true</owl:deprecated>
      </skos:Concept>
    </skos:related>

    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EiraArchitectureBuildingBlock_Properties</dc:identifier>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EiraView_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of EIRA View</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of EIRA View</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:EiraView</dc:type>
    <eira:ABB_Status>Obsolete</eira:ABB_Status>
    <eira:ID>ABB336</eira:ID>
    <owl:deprecated>true</owl:deprecated>
    <skos:related>
      <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EiraView">
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">DEFINITION:
EIRA view ABB is a Business Object containing a graphical notation of the EIRA ontology. The EIRA consists of several architecture views (1) , including one view for each of the EIF interoperability levels.

(1) An architecture view is a representation of a system from the perspective of a related set of concerns.

Source: TOGAF (&lt;a href=&quot;https://pubs.opengroup.org/architecture/togaf9-doc/arch/chap03.html#tag_03_17&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://pubs.opengroup.org/architecture/togaf9-doc/arch/chap03.html#tag…&lt;/a&gt;)

EXAMPLES:
The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB):

Legal View
The Legal view models the most salient public policy development enablers and implementation instruments that shall be considered in order to support the End to End design of interoperable digital public services.</skos:definition>
        <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">EIRA View</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Deprecated"/>
        <owl:deprecated>true</owl:deprecated>
      </skos:Concept>
    </skos:related>

    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EiraView_Properties</dc:identifier>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EiraViewpoint_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of EIRA Viewpoint</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of EIRA Viewpoint</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:EiraViewpoint</dc:type>
    <eira:ID>ABB333</eira:ID>
    <eira:ABB_Status>Obsolete</eira:ABB_Status>
    <owl:deprecated>true</owl:deprecated>
    <skos:related>
      <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EiraViewpoint">
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">DEFINITION:
EIRA viewpoint ABB is a Business Object providing a perspective with specific stakeholders concern in mind. The EIRA© provides several viewpoints that conform to EIRA© views

(1) A specification of the conventions for a particular kind of architecture view.

Source: TOGAF (&lt;a href=&quot;https://pubs.opengroup.org/architecture/togaf9-doc/arch/chap03.html#tag_03_18&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://pubs.opengroup.org/architecture/togaf9-doc/arch/chap03.html#tag…&lt;/a&gt;)

EXAMPLES:
The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB):

Highlevel viewpoint
The EIRA© Highlevel viewpoint models an introductory overview of the focal Architecture Building Blocks of each view. It aligns the EIRA© with the service delivery model described within the Interoperability Maturity Model  (IMM), and the New European Interoperability Framework (EIF) conceptual model for public services.
The ABBs included in the high-level viewpoint represent the points that link the EIRA©’s views enabling traceability between their different Architecture Building Blocks. They are not necessarily mandatory but should always be considered by a user of the EIRA© when executing one of its use cases.</skos:definition>
        <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">EIRA Viewpoint</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Deprecated"/>
        <owl:deprecated>true</owl:deprecated>
      </skos:Concept>
    </skos:related>

    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EiraViewpoint_Properties</dc:identifier>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EnterpriseServiceBusTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-23</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Enterprise Service Bus ABB is a Technology Service that enables integration between applications by acting as a centralized component to perform the transformation in data models, handle connectivity, perform message routing, convert communication protocols and manage the composition of multiple requests.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Enterprise Service Bus</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Enterprise Service Bus</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:EnterpriseServiceBusTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): eXTra Enterprise Service Bus (eESB), eESB is an Enterprise Service Bus for exchanging data between the institutes of the German pension insurance. To connect the services within one institute EJB-Technology is used. The communication with external partners and between the different institutes of the German pension insurance is based on SOAP-WebServices. As data structure for the general communication the eXTra-Standard is used to address the responsible service applications. https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/egovernment/solution/extra-enterprise-service-bus-eesb/about</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EnterpriseServiceBusTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>Gartner</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Enterprise Service Bus ABB is salient for semantic and technical interoperability due to it ensuring (i) data sharing across different public service applications and infrastructures using specific enhanced datasets with metadata, and (ii) providing data sharing mechanism using open specifications and open data standards.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EnterpriseServiceBusTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EnterpriseServiceBusTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EnterpriseServiceBusTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.gartner.com/en/documents/1405237</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/EuropeanDIgitalSovereignty_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of European digital sovereignty</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of European digital sovereignty</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:EuropeanDIgitalSovereignty</dc:type>
    <eira:ID>ABB417</eira:ID>
