  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentityAndAccessInfrastructureEnablers_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Identity and Access Infrastructure Enablers</skos:notation>
    <skos:definition>Identity and Access Infrastructure Enablers ABB is a Grouìng of a set of components and services that provide the underlying functionality to implement identity and access management solutions</skos:definition>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Identity and Access Infrastructure Enablers</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:IdentityAndAccessInfrastructureEnablers</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Lightweight Directory Access Protocol can be implemented in multiple platforms or systems, allowing to integrating an organisatio'n LDAP-enabled identity management service to other platforms such as Drupal. https://www.drupal.org/docs/contributed-modules/lightweight-directory-access-protocol-ldap</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentityAndAccessInfrastructureEnablers</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in CAMSS</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Identity and Access Infrastructure Enablers ABB is Salient for the technical, organizational and semantic interoperability because it provides (i) the setup and implementation of rules to access public services, (ii) the tools and mechanism to identify unequivocally organizations or individuals, (iii) the tools and mechanisms to facilitate the access and use of the public services</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentityAndAccessInfrastructureEnablers"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentityAndAccessInfrastructureEnablers</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentityAndAccessInfrastructureEnablers_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/common-assessment-method-standards-and-specifications-camss</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentityMangementApplicationService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-18</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Identity Management ABB is an Application Service that enables the set of processes, policies and technologies used to manage and secure digital entities of individuals, devices and applications.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Identity management</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Identity management</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:IdentityMangementApplicationService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): EU Login - EU Login is the European Commission's user authentication service. It allows authorised users to access a wide range of Commission web services. EU Login is the entry gate to sign in to different European Commission services and/or other systems. EU Login verifies your identity and allows recovering your personal settings, history and access rights in a secure way. You can sign in using social media accounts or the EU Login account. EU Login supports a variety of verification methods: • Password; • ECAS Mobile App PIN code; • ECAS Mobile App QR code; • On mobile authentication; • Mobile phone + SMS; • Token and Token CRAM. https://webgate.ec.europa.eu/cas/manuals/EU_Login_Tutorial_1.1.pdf</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentityMangementApplicationService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in eIDAS</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Identity Management Application Service is salient for interoperability because it can help in the management of digital identities for individuals, devices and applications, ensuring and enabling that information on digital public services is available under the proper conditions and to the specific target. This can ensure and enhance the quality of data meant to be exchanged through interoperable systems, applications and digital public services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentityMangementApplicationService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32014R0910&amp;from=EN</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentityMangementApplicationService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentityMangementApplicationService</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentityProviderTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Identity Provider</skos:notation>
    <skos:definition>Identity provider ABB is a Technology Service that enables the authentication of users and provides them with a secure means of accessing online resources and applications</skos:definition>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Identity Provider</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:IdentityProviderTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): EU Login is the European Commission's user authentication service. It allows authorised users to access a wide range of Commission web services. EU Login is the entry gate to sign in to different European Commission services and/or other systems. EU Login verifies your identity and allows recovering your personal settings, history and access rights in a secure way. You can sign in using social media accounts or the EU Login account.  https://webgate.ec.europa.eu/cas/about.html</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentityProviderTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inpired in eIDAS</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Identity Provider ABB is salient for technical and semantic interoperability because it provides mechanisms to ensure the identification of stakeholders (organizations or individuals) across multiple platforms around Europe. Thus, it permits: (i) making interoperable identities across the public service platforms, and (ii) secure identification to the public services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentityProviderTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eidas-regulation</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentityProviderTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IdentityProviderTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

