  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IndividualStakeholder_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-12-1</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Individual</skos:notation>
    <skos:definition>Individual ABB is a Stakeholder that is a human being who may be dead or alive, but not imaginary.</skos:definition>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Individual</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:IndividualStakeholder</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Any instance of a person, for instance, Ursula von der Leyen, President of the European Commission. https://ec.europa.eu/commission/commissioners/2019-2024/president_en</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IndividualStakeholder</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>SEMIC-CPV</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:synonym>Person</eira:synonym>
    <eira:viewpoint>Interoperability Privacy viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Individual ABB is salient for organizational and behavioural interoperability because it permits the identification of procedures and business rules related to this stakeholder that facilitates the exchange of data, information and knowledge between digital public services and individuals (and vice versa).</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IndividualStakeholder"/>
    <eira:view>Organisational view</eira:view>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://semiceu.github.io/Core-Person-Vocabulary/releases/2.00/#Person</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IndividualStakeholder</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/IndividualStakeholder_Properties</dc:identifier>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/InformationBusinessObject_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-11-1</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Information</skos:notation>
    <skos:definition>Information ABB is a Business Object describing business facts, assets, or opinions that are exchanged in the context of a digital public service to support its delivery. Information is enacted via interpretation rules (expressed in an ontology) of data and considering knowledge of a given context. Examples include an invoice, a medical prescription, a driving license.</skos:definition>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Information</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:InformationBusinessObject</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Surveillance3 - Surveillance information: Published Surveillance information (Business Information) on Europa: Textile category 1 - Cotton yarn, not put up for retail sale [Council Regulation (EEC) No 3030/93] from Belarus in 2015: see URL for details(http://ec.europa.eu/taxation_customs/dds2/surv/surv_data_list.jsp?Lang=en&amp;survNumber=670010&amp;survType=1&amp;startDate=20150101&amp;originCode=BY)</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/InformationBusinessObject</eira:PURI>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>TOGAF guide about business capabilities, TOGAF definition of information</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:viewpoint>Highlevel viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:viewpoint>Interoperability Privacy viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:synonym>Business Facts, Business Data, Business Opinions</eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Information ABB  is salient for organisational interoperability because it represents the data being exchanged between organisations. Its interoperability needs to be guaranteed using organisational and semantic interoperability specifications.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/InformationBusinessObject"/>
    <eira:view>Organisational view</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/InformationBusinessObject_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/InformationBusinessObject</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>(https://www2.opengroup.org/ogsys/catalog/g161)), (http://pubs.opengroup.org/architecture/togaf9-doc/arch/)</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/InmutableDatabaseManagerTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Inmutable Database Manager</skos:notation>
    <skos:definition>Immutable Database Manager ABB is a Technology Service that enables the procedure to manage data that cannot be (or shouldn't be) deleted or modified.</skos:definition>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Inmutable Database Manager</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:InmutableDatabaseManagerTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): immubd is a database written in Go, but unlike other databases, it is immutable: history is preserved and can't be changed without clients noticing. immudb can be used both as a key-value store, or as a relational database (SQL). immudb can be run as full database server with replicas or easily embedded as a lightweight database into application. https://docs.immudb.io/master/</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/InmutableDatabaseManagerTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>ODBMS</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Immutable Database Manager ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it establishes the mechanism to store information and also, manages that the stored information is cannot be deleted or modified.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/InmutableDatabaseManagerTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.odbms.org/2015/10/the-rise-of-immutable-data-stores/</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/InmutableDatabaseManagerTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/InmutableDatabaseManagerTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Innovation_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Innovation</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
