  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/PublicCloudComputingFacility">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Definition: Public Cloud Computing Facility ABB is a Facility that enables a cloud infrastructure that is shared among multiple users and organizations and is typically managed by a third-party service provider

Source: Inpired in Redhat

Source reference: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.redhat.com/en/topics/cloud-computing/public-cloud-vs-private-cloud-and-hybrid-cloud&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://www.redhat.com/en/topics/cloud-computing/public-cloud-vs-privat…&lt;/a&gt;

Example: The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): JRC- Development of the EU Green Public Procurement (GPP)- Critaria for Data Centres, Server Rooms and Cloud Services. &lt;a href=&quot;https://ec.europa.eu/environment/gpp/pdf/jrc118558_2020_0605_data_centres_technical_report_jrc_clean_with_id.pdf&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://ec.europa.eu/environment/gpp/pdf/jrc118558_2020_0605_data_centr…&lt;/a&gt;

LOST view: Technical view - Infrastructure

Interoperability saliency: Public Cloud Facilities ABB is salient for organizational and technical interoperability because it establishes the business rules and responsibilities to deploy and deliver public administration services remotely.

