  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustInfrastructureEnablers">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Definition: Trust Infrastructure Enablers ABB is a Grouping of a set of components and services devoted  to creating and managing public keys for encryption, which is a common method of securing data transfers on the internet

Source: ENISA

Source reference: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.enisa.europa.eu/topics/incident-response/glossary/public-key-infrastructure-pki&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://www.enisa.europa.eu/topics/incident-response/glossary/public-ke…&lt;/a&gt;

Synonym:

Additional information:

Example: The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): eDelivery - PKI Service. &lt;a href=&quot;https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/display/DIGITAL/PKI+Service&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/display/DIGITAL/PKI+…&lt;/a&gt;

IoP Dimension:

