  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/LegalClausesRequirement">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Definition: Legal clauses ABB is a Requirement that refers to specific points or topics that permit to specify a legal document.

Source: European Comision

Source reference: &lt;a href=&quot;https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/types-eu-law_en&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://commission.europa.eu/law/law-making-process/types-eu-law_en&lt;/a&gt;

Example: The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Clause 6 - Description of the transfer(s): The details of the transfer(s), and in particular the categories of personal data that are transferred and the purpose(s) for which they are transferred, are specified in Annex I.B. (&lt;a href=&quot;http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2021/914/oj&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2021/914/oj&lt;/a&gt;)

LOST view: Legal view

