  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/RouterTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Router ABB is a Technology Service that enables the implementation of a component to connect multiple networks and directs traffic between them</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Router</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Router</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:RouterTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/RouterTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Turris Omnia Open Source Router, https://opensource.com/article/22/1/turris-omnia-open-source-router</skos:example>
    <eira:definitionSource>ISO 35.110</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Router ABB is salient for technical interoperability due to it physically establishes the rules for distributing the information into a network.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/RouterTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/RouterTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/RouterTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.iso.org/ics/35.110/x/</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/SaasTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-31</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>SaaS ABB is a Technology Service that enables the procedures for delivering software that is owned and managed remotely by one or more providers. The provider delivers software based on one set of common code and data definitions that is consumed in a one-to-many model by all contracted customers at any time on a pay-for-use basis or as a subscription based on use metrics.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Saas</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Saas</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:SaasTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/SaasTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Drupal is content management software. It's used to make many of the websites and applications you use every day. Drupal has great standard features, like easy content authoring, reliable performance, and excellent security. But what sets it apart is its flexibility; modularity is one of its core principles. Its tools help you build the versatile, structured content that dynamic web experiences need. https://www.drupal.org/about</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>Gartner</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The SaaS ABB is salient for organizational, semantic and technical and technical interoperability due to it provides the needed infrastructure to deliver public administration services on demand. Also, SaaS provides the functionalities of common data models and definitions to support the internal communication between software components. Finally, SaaS provides also the set up of business rules to ensure the correct performance of the software modules.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/SaasTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/SaasTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/SaasTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.gartner.com/en/information-technology/glossary/software-as-a-service-saas</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ScheduleManagementApplicationComponent_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Schedule Management Component ABB is an Application Component that enables the implementation of the procedures to manage time and events in the achievement of the goals and delivery of public services.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Schedule Management</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Schedule Management</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:ScheduleManagementApplicationComponent</dc:type>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ScheduleManagementApplicationComponent</eira:PURI>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Chronos is a replacement for cron. It is a distributed and fault-tolerant scheduler that runs on top of Apache Mesos that can be used for job orchestration. It supports custom Mesos executors as well as the default command executor. Thus by default, Chronos executes sh (on most systems bash) scripts. https://sourceforge.net/projects/chronos.mirror/</skos:example>
    <eira:iopDimension>Governance IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in Public Works and Goverment Services Canada</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Schedule Management Application Component ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it implements the orchestration of different events within digital public services within specific platforms but can be reused and extended in a high-level approach to enable interoperability of digital public services and the different delivery models.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ScheduleManagementApplicationComponent"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ScheduleManagementApplicationComponent</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ScheduleManagementApplicationComponent_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://buyandsell.gc.ca/cds/public/2016/11/23/c7b27e0ac41ad50ffae2f12b0a837875/ABES.PROD.PW_PWZ.B014.E10051.ATTA001.PDF</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ScheduleManagementApplicationService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Schedule Management Service ABB is an Application Service that enables the procedures to manage time and events in the achievement of the goals and delivery of public services.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Schedule Management</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Schedule Management</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:ScheduleManagementApplicationService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Chronos is a replacement for cron. It is a distributed and fault-tolerant scheduler that runs on top of Apache Mesos that can be used for job orchestration. It supports custom Mesos executors as well as the default command executor. Thus by default, Chronos executes sh (on most systems bash) scripts. https://sourceforge.net/projects/chronos.mirror/</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ScheduleManagementApplicationService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in Public Works and Goverment Services Canada</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Schedule Management Application Service ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it allows managing and orchestrating different events physical and digital ones within a determined workflow according to the delivery model of each digital public service.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ScheduleManagementApplicationService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ScheduleManagementApplicationService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ScheduleManagementApplicationService</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://buyandsell.gc.ca/cds/public/2016/11/23/c7b27e0ac41ad50ffae2f12b0a837875/ABES.PROD.PW_PWZ.B014.E10051.ATTA001.PDF</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ScheduleManagementEnablersGrouping_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Schedule Management Enablers ABB is a Grouping that enables the implementation of components and services to create, distribute and manage events at different scales inside a cloud platform.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Schedule Management Enablers</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Schedule Management Enablers</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:ScheduleManagementEnablersGrouping</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Chronos is a replacement for cron. It is a distributed and fault-tolerant scheduler that runs on top of Apache Mesos that can be used for job orchestration. It supports custom Mesos executors as well as the default command executor. Thus by default, Chronos executes sh (on most systems bash) scripts. https://sourceforge.net/projects/chronos.mirror/</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ScheduleManagementEnablersGrouping</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in Redhat</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Schedule Management Enablers Grouping ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it comprises the different services and tools that allow to organise and manage events within a platform for the delivery of a digital public service. It enables interoperability by allowing the management of events through a single point of access (for users and administrations) and the reuse of such information to an overall relationship between public administration and stakeholders.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ScheduleManagementEnablersGrouping"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ScheduleManagementEnablersGrouping_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ScheduleManagementEnablersGrouping</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.redhat.com/en/topics/cloud-computing/what-is-cloud-management</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/SchemaLevelMapping_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Schema Level Mapping</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Schema Level Mapping</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:SchemaLevelMapping</dc:type>
