    <owl:deprecated>true</owl:deprecated>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Transparency"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Transparency_Properties</dc:identifier>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustEnablersGrouping_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Trust Enablers ABB is a Grouping that refers to components and services that facilitate the establishment and maintenance of secure-cross borders transactions and interactions.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Trust Enablers</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Trust Enablers</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:TrustEnablersGrouping</dc:type>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustEnablersGrouping</eira:PURI>
    <skos:example></skos:example>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in eIDAS</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Trust Enablers Grouping is salient for interoperability because it comprises the set of tools, services and applications that allow to secure the digital public services across borders. Trust enablers are focused on transactions and interactions between parties (services, platforms, individuals) related to services. By applying those mechanisms identities, and timestamps (amongst other aspects) can be guaranteed and ensure the trustworthy data exchange</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustEnablersGrouping"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustEnablersGrouping</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustEnablersGrouping_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=uriserv%3AOJ.L_.2014.257.01.0073.01.ENG</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustInfrastructureEnablers_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Trust Infrastructure Enablers ABB is a Grouping of a set of components and services devoted  to creating and managing public keys for encryption, which is a common method of securing data transfers on the internet</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Trust Infrastructure Enablers</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Trust Infrastructure Enablers</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:TrustInfrastructureEnablers</dc:type>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustInfrastructureEnablers</eira:PURI>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): eDelivery - PKI Service. https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/wikis/display/DIGITAL/PKI+Service</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>ENISA</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Trust Infrastructure Enablers ABB is salient for organizational interoperability because it defines the rules and methodologies to ensure the secure and trustworthy exchange of information between public services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustInfrastructureEnablers"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustInfrastructureEnablers</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustInfrastructureEnablers_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.enisa.europa.eu/topics/incident-response/glossary/public-key-infrastructure-pki</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustServiceProvisioningApplicationComponent_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-20</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Trust Service Provisioning ABB is an Application Component that enables the creation, verification, or validation of electronic signatures, time stamps, seals, electronically registered delivery services, and certificates.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Trust Service Provisioning</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Trust Service Provisioning</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:TrustServiceProvisioningApplicationComponent</dc:type>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustServiceProvisioningApplicationComponent</eira:PURI>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): e-TrustEx - Open e-TrustEx is a platform offered by the Directorate-General for Informatics of the European Commission to Public Administrations at European, national and regional level to set up secure exchange of natively digital documents from system to system via standardized interfaces. Open e-TrustEx provides a set of generic web services, which Public Administrations can use to connect heterogeneous applications, removing the need for complex point-to-point connections. http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/DE/TXT/?uri=CELEX%3A52016SC0279</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>eIDAS</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Trust Service Provisioning Component ABB  is salient for technical interoperability  because it provides the implementation of the functionalities of information exchange between between administrations, businesses and citizens (e-signature and e-seal creation, verification,validation and preservation, timestamping  creation, verification and validation, identity management, etc.) as stated in the EIF recommendation n°47: &quot;Use trust services according to the Regulation on eID and Trust Services as mechanisms that ensure secure and protected data exchange in public services.&quot;</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:viewpoint>Interoperability Security viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustServiceProvisioningApplicationComponent"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustServiceProvisioningApplicationComponent</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TrustServiceProvisioningApplicationComponent_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>http://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=uriserv%3AOJ.L_.2014.257.01.0073.01.ENG</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note>A ‘trust service’ means an electronic service normally provided for remuneration which consists of these functionalities: i) the creation, verification, and validation of electronic signatures, electronic seals or electronic time stamps, electronic registered delivery services and certificates related to those services, or; ii) the creation, verification and validation of certificates for website authentication; or; iii) the preservation of electronic signatures, seals or certificates related to those services.</skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Trust_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Trust</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Trust</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:Trust</dc:type>
    <eira:ABB_Status>Obsolete</eira:ABB_Status>
    <eira:ID>ABB388</eira:ID>
    <owl:deprecated>true</owl:deprecated>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Trust"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Trust_Properties</dc:identifier>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/UXManagementApplicationService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-23</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>UX Management Service ABB is Application Service managing user experience design-related activities inside an organization to create growth and good management practices. Typical UX management activities are to define an organization’s UX design language and strategy and manage the work processes around UX design.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of UX Management</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of UX Management</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:UXManagementApplicationService</dc:type>
    <skos:example></skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/UXManagementApplicationService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>Interaction design</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopSaliency>UX Management ABB is a key interoperability enabler (*) for behavioural interoperability, governance and semantic interoperability by enabling (i) a set of rules and best practices for user experience with public service components; (ii) a set of indicators to monitor and understand usability in public services; and (ii) metadata information to understand the visual elements of the public service components</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:viewpoint>Key Interoperability Enablers viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/UXManagementApplicationService"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/UXManagementApplicationService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/UXManagementApplicationService</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>(https://www.interaction-design.org/literature/topics/ux-management)</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/User-centricity_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:notation>Properties of User-centricity</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of User-centricity</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:User-centricity</dc:type>
    <eira:ABB_Status>Obsolete</eira:ABB_Status>
    <eira:ID>ABB405</eira:ID>
    <owl:deprecated>true</owl:deprecated>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/User-centricity"/>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/User-centricity_Properties</dc:identifier>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/UserExperienceManagementEnablersGrouping_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>User Experience Management Enablers ABB is a Grouping that refers to components and services that track, measure, analyze and improve any interaction people have with the organization</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of User Experience Management Enablers</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of User Experience Management Enablers</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:UserExperienceManagementEnablersGrouping</dc:type>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/UserExperienceManagementEnablersGrouping</eira:PURI>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Mi Carpeta Ciudadana Carpeta Ciudadana is a personal online space that facilitates your relationship with public administrations. https://carpetaciudadana.gob.es/carpeta/clave.htm</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inpired in referece business and cloud provider compabies</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The User Experience Management Enablers Grouping ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it comprises services and components that allow different parties involved in the use and delivery o public services, to exchange and provide data or information.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/UserExperienceManagementEnablersGrouping"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/UserExperienceManagementEnablersGrouping_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/UserExperienceManagementEnablersGrouping</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.vmware.com/topics/glossary/content/experience-management.html</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/VirtualDatasetDataObject_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-16</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Virtual Dataset ABB is a Data Object that enables a dynamic and logical representation of data that aggregates, integrates, or transforms data from multiple sources into a single view</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Virtual Dataset</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Virtual Dataset</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:VirtualDatasetDataObject</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Virtual Datasets (VDS) is an example of a distribution for the creation of virtual datasets. https://docs.h5py.org/en/stable/vds.html</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/VirtualDatasetDataObject</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>H5PY</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:viewpoint>Interoperability Privacy viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Virtual Dataset Data Object ABB is salient for semantic interoperability due to its position on and capability for transforming data from different and multiple channels to a single view allowing and increasing the reuse and shareability of data across organisations and digital public services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/VirtualDatasetDataObject"/>
    <eira:view>Semantic view</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/VirtualDatasetDataObject</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/VirtualDatasetDataObject_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://docs.h5py.org/en/stable/vds.html</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/VirtualMachineNode_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-31</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Virtual Machine ABB is a Node that enables the emulation of a physical computer to run programs and deploy applications.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Virtual Machine</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Virtual Machine</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:VirtualMachineNode</dc:type>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/VirtualMachineNode</eira:PURI>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Redhat Virtualization: Built on Red Hat Enterprise Linux® and KVM and fully maintained by Red Hat, Red Hat® Virtualization is an enterprise virtualization platform that supports core virtualization workloads, including resource-intensive and important applications. With a solid foundation for a cloud-native and containerized future, virtualize your resources, workflows, and software applications. Additionally compatible with platforms like Microsoft Exchange and the Oracle database is Red Hat Enterprise Virtualization. https://www.redhat.com/en/technologies/virtualization/enterprise-virtualization</skos:example>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in Redhat</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Virtual Machine ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it provides needed tools to emulate the public administration services under controlled environments.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/VirtualMachineNode"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/VirtualMachineNode</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/VirtualMachineNode_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.redhat.com/en/topics/virtualization/what-is-a-virtual-machine</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/VirtualPrivateNetworkTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Virtual Private Network ABB is a Technology Service that enables the procedures to implement a protected information system link utilizing tunnelling, security controls, and endpoint address translation giving the impression of a dedicated line</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Virtual Private Network</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Virtual Private Network</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:VirtualPrivateNetworkTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Virtual Private Network service for accessing European Commission servers out of the Commission. https://wikis.ec.europa.eu/display/WEBGUIDE/01.+Access+to+servers+from+outside+the+European+Commission</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/VirtualPrivateNetworkTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>NIST</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Virtual Private Network ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it implements standard methods to build a secure network to exchange information in public administration</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/VirtualPrivateNetworkTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/VirtualPrivateNetworkTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/VirtualPrivateNetworkTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://csrc.nist.gov/glossary/term/virtual_private_network</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebPortalBusinessInterface_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-20</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Web APP ABB is a Business Interface that corresponds to a computer program that runs on a web browser and is accessible through the internet</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Web App</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Web App</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:WebPortalBusinessInterface</dc:type>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebPortalBusinessInterface</eira:PURI>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Digital Signature Service (DSS) Web Application. https://ec.europa.eu/digital-building-blocks/DSS/webapp-demo/home</skos:example>
    <eira:definitionSource>ISO/IEC/IEEE 23026:2015</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Web App ABB is salient for organizational, semantic and technical interoperability because it offers (i) a visual environment to interact with the public service procedures and data; (ii) an understanding of the information to be represented; and (iii) an elaborate mechanism to exchange data with public services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebPortalBusinessInterface"/>
    <eira:view>Organisational view</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebPortalBusinessInterface_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebPortalBusinessInterface</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#iso:std:iso-iec-ieee:23026:ed-1:v1:en</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebServerTechnologyService_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Web Server ABB is a Technology Service that implements the behaviour of a type of server software that handles HTTP (Hypertext Transfer Protocol) requests sent by clients, typically web browsers, and delivers web content back to the client in response</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Web Server</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Web Server</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:WebServerTechnologyService</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): DIGIT/C Hosting Service - DIGIT/C offers a high availability and high performance hosting infrastructure that is being comprised, among other elements, of back-end web server instances and application servers for hosting and serving both static and dynamic sites. http://ec.europa.eu/ipg/build/infrastructure/index_en.htm</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebServerTechnologyService</eira:PURI>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in ISA2-EIF</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Streaming Server is salient for semantic technical interoperability because it provides ICT systems to manage data streams related to public digital services. This ABB provides real-time interaction with the data following up streaming open specifications and metadata (if needed).</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebServerTechnologyService"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebServerTechnologyService</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebServerTechnologyService_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://eur-lex.europa.eu/resource.html?uri=cellar:2c2f2554-0faf-11e7-8a35-01aa75ed71a1.0017.02/DOC_1&amp;format=PDF</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebServiceApplicationInterface_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2022-01-18</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Web Service ABB is an Application Interface that enables interoperability between different applications or systems over the Internet</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Web Service</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Web Service</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:WebServiceApplicationInterface</dc:type>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Web Services Description Language (WSDL) - WSDL is an XML format for describing network services as a set of endpoints operating on messages containing either document-oriented or procedure-oriented information. The operations and messages are described abstractly, and then bound to a concrete network protocol and message format to define an endpoint. https://www.w3.org/TR/wsdl.html</skos:example>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebServiceApplicationInterface</eira:PURI>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>W3C</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopSaliency>The Web Service Application Interface ABB is salient for interoperability because, from the beginning, Web services can be interoperable by design. By putting in place web services, interoperability can be guaranteed between systems and applications, and therefore, among digital public services.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopDimension>Behavioral IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebServiceApplicationInterface"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebServiceApplicationInterface</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebServiceApplicationInterface_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.w3.org/TR/2004/NOTE-ws-arch-20040211/#relwwwrest</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WorkflowOrchestrationInfrastructureEnablers_Properties">
    <dc:modified>2023-05-25</dc:modified>
    <skos:definition>Workflow Orchestration Infrastructure Enablers ABB is a Grouping that refers to components and services that enable the coordination and automation of components through workflows across multiple systems, applications, and organizations.</skos:definition>
    <skos:notation>Properties of Workflow Orchestration Infrastructure Enablers</skos:notation>
    <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Properties of Workflow Orchestration Infrastructure Enablers</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:type>eira:WorkflowOrchestrationInfrastructureEnablers</dc:type>
    <eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WorkflowOrchestrationInfrastructureEnablers</eira:PURI>
    <skos:example>The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): UNDP- Business Process Re-engineering Manual. https://www.undp.org/sites/g/files/zskgke326/files/migration/uz/BPR-Manual_designed---Eng---final.pdf</skos:example>
    <eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
    <eira:definitionSource>Inspired in Redhat</eira:definitionSource>
    <eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
    <eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
    <eira:iopSaliency>Process Orchestration Infrastructure Enablers ABB is salient for organizational interoperability because it implements and defines the rules to manage different public administration services and matchmake the processes to provide effective responses to the public administration consumers.</eira:iopSaliency>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WorkflowOrchestrationInfrastructureEnablers"/>
    <eira:view>Technical view - infrastructure</eira:view>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WorkflowOrchestrationInfrastructureEnablers</dc:identifier>
    <dc:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WorkflowOrchestrationInfrastructureEnablers_Properties</dc:identifier>
    <eira:definitionSourceReference>https://www.redhat.com/en/topics/automation/what-is-orchestration</eira:definitionSourceReference>
    <skos:note></skos:note>
  </skos:Concept>

